; makefile.link: the PSYLINK 2.52 link script of the 13 PlayStation programs of SLUS-00747 (USA), linked in ONE run, as bio2-ds does:
; the main program SLUS_007.47 (the groups text and bss, written to the CPE) and the 12 PROG2 overlays, one group each, written to
; their own file("...") images. tools\cpe2exe.exe turns the CPE and each image into a PS-X EXE.
;
; The names between two at signs are placeholders that tools\gen_linkscript.exe fills in right before the run (PSYLINK has no
; variables): the PSY-Q locations from tools\sdkroot.ini, and from the makefile OBJ (the compiled objects), OVL (the objects of the
; overlays, see below) and LINK (the folder the images are written to).
;
; Overlays share one name space with everything else in one run, but the game's overlays are separate programs that load at the same
; address and use the same names (the stage code of zombie, hunter, crow, ... exists once per stage; every overlay links the SDK
; startup object NONE2.OBJ). So each overlay's objects are made distinct first:
;   - the sections are named per overlay, STAGE3.text, STAGE3.data, ... (cc263 -sSTAGE3, i.e. ASPSX -sSTAGE3, as bio2-ds does), and
;   - tools\ovlprefix.exe gives the overlay's global names the prefix of the overlay (Em06_Move_dodge -> STAGE3_Em06_Move_dodge) and
;     NONE2.OBJ both the prefix and the sections. The copies are in the OVL folder, one subfolder per overlay; no name is part of
;     an executable.
; An overlay's entry point is its STAGE3___SN_ENTRY_POINT.
;
; Groups: an overlay is one group, .sbss/.bss after .data/.sdata like every other section. The executable does not store the
; uninitialised data (the startup code clears it at run time), so tools\cpe2exe.exe ends the image where the map puts the
; overlay's .sbss or .bss. (The main program keeps .sbss/.bss in a group of their own, which the CPE leaves out.)

; SLUS_007.47: the main executable (49 units + PsyQ libraries)
; The address of its bss group is the end of the stored data (.data/.sdata of the main program); it is written out because PSYLINK
; cannot compute it. If the data size changes, update it: the build ends with a check against retail, which flags a wrong one.

	org	0x80010000
	regs	pc=__SN_ENTRY_POINT

text	group	obj(0x80010000)
bss	group	bss,obj(0x800B235C)

	section .rdata,text
	section .text,text
	section .ctors,text
	section .dtors,text
	section .data,text
	section .sdata,text
	section .sbss,bss
	section .bss,bss

