; BSS order. PSYLINK allocates COMMON symbols by a hash of the name (sum of the bytes + length, mod 512), plain ones before aliased ones of the same
; hash, and the aliased ones of a hash in the reverse order of these lines. The game's own names are free, so every common whose retail position
; came from a name now carries a key here: `Pos_x alias Name` places Name where a name with the hash of Pos_x would be. The lines are fitted, not
; recovered names. A self alias (`X alias X`) only moves an SDK or other symbol behind the aliased ones of its hash; the remaining lines
; (POSITION, SpuCommonError, ...) give a second name to a common.
_TITLE_rdata_org	alias	_TITLE_rdata_org
_PROLOGUE_sbss_orgend	alias	_PROLOGUE_sbss_orgend
_PROLOGUE_data_orgend	alias	_PROLOGUE_data_orgend
_LOGO_sdata_orgend	alias	_LOGO_sdata_orgend
_LOGO_org	alias	_LOGO_org
